 "units": "mm",
 "comment": "Tilting TV wall mount (from a photo). The tilt joint pivots on the lower knob P; the upper knob K, clamped in an arc slot of radius r, holds the tilt by friction F_f. The wall plate is held by two screws h apart. Wall is x = 0, x points out of the wall, z up. The TV is drawn cut beside the mount so the joint stays visible. All sizes are estimated from the photo (VESA plate taken as 200 mm wide).",
